-- title:
--   Scheme points over a π-adically complete local ring
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring, $\pi\in\mathcal O$, and let $R$ be a local commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra which is adically complete for the ideal $I=(\pi_R)$ generated by the image $\pi_R=\operatorname{algebraMap}_{\mathcal O,R}(\pi)$ (Hausdorff and precomplete for the $I$-adic filtration). Write $\mathrm{modPow}\,\pi\,R\,n$ for the quotient $R/(\pi_R^{\,n+1})$ by the ideal generated by the single element $\pi_R^{\,n+1}$, and $\mathrm{modPowTransition}\,\pi\,R\,n$ for the induced $\mathcal O$-algebra surjection $R/(\pi_R^{\,n+2})\to R/(\pi_R^{\,n+1})$. Let $X$ be a scheme (in the bottom universe) and let $x_n\colon \operatorname{Spec}\bigl(R/(\pi_R^{\,n+1})\bigr)\to X$ be a family of morphisms, one for each $n\in\mathbb N$, compatible in the sense that for every $n$ the morphism $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the transition map followed by $x_{n+1}$ equals $x_n$. Then there is exactly one morphism $y\colon\operatorname{Spec} R\to X$ such that for every $n$ the morphism $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the quotient map $R\to R/(\pi_R^{\,n+1})$ followed by $y$ equals $x_n$.
--
--   This is the representability of an $R$-point of an arbitrary scheme by its system of truncations, in the form needed for principal powers $(\pi^{n+1})$: a compatible family of $R/\pi^{n+1}$-points of $X$ over a local $\pi$-adically complete base glues to a unique $R$-point. It is used to produce integral points of the Čerednik–Drinfeld quotient from their truncations, and hence in the identification of the germs of the function field at such points.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalOmega_existsUnique_hom_comp_eq_of_compatible_modPow.lean

